{"name":"Beige Red","hex":"#de9408","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Klaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg/500px-Klaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Klaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg/500px-Klaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKlaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg/500px-1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg/1280px-1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg/500px-1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Coloured_beige_vinyl_%28Funkadelic_-_Maggot_Brain_-_reissue_code_HIQLP_020%29.jpg/500px-Coloured_beige_vinyl_%28Funkadelic_-_Maggot_Brain_-_reissue_code_HIQLP_020%29.jpg?utm_source=en.w